.env
.env.*
!.env.example

__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Local browser profiles, if you ever test the daemon on the workstation
.local/
profiles/
shell/

# Service logos are trademarked brand assets and are fetched per machine into
# ~/.local/share/pilauncher/logos, never committed. This catches one dropped
# into the repo root by mistake on its way to the Pi.
*.svg
*.png
*.webp
*.jpg
*.jpeg

# Not every image here is a stray, though. pimedia-splash-source.png is DJ's
# own "Pi Media by StrangeCraft" artwork, the source for the custom page on the
# Pironman case OLED. It is deliberately kept and deliberately untracked, so do
# not delete it as clutter. Being ignored, git is NOT a backup of it.

# Working folder for service logo artwork on its way to the Pi. The file rules
# above already catch every image type in it; the folder is named here as well
# because its whole contents are other people's trademarks and one rule is a
# thin margin for that on a public repository.
app-logos/

# design/ is the brand kit: the marks, the tokens and the sheet they are
# documented on. The rule above exists to catch a service logo dropped in on
# its way to the Pi, which is the opposite of this. The launcher inlines these
# marks rather than fetching them, so the folder is reference rather than a
# runtime dependency, and it is the source of truth for both.
!design/
!design/*

# screenshots/ is the shipped documentation for the README. Same reasoning as
# design/: these are pictures of this project, not somebody's brand asset
# waiting to be copied to the Pi.
!screenshots/
!screenshots/*


# Predecessor LineageOS ROM, Magisk, gapps and widevine zips (~1GB). Kept for
# reference, never part of the launcher.
Lineage/

# Sideloaded Android packages staged for Waydroid. Large, and not source.
*.apk
*.apkm
*.xapk
